  "verdict": "INTERNAL_CODE_ACCEPT",
  "verdictSummary": "Narrow INTERNAL_CODE_ACCEPT of the pure private D04 seam at 08e0 against the accepted Rev3 design and the Root implementation grant. One LOW (D04-L1, fail-closed stage/reason placement of the signature-tuple-table bound, non-blocking, correct in the next code cut) and four INFO. No HIGH/MEDIUM. No positive path differs from the design: every reviewer-found divergence refuses in both. Scope is INTERNAL_CODE only; Core 42287980945 is still PENDING, and integration, runtime, producer/auth and fleet acceptance are separate axes not granted here.",
  "findings": [
    {
      "id": "D04-L1", "severity": "LOW", "blocking": false, "kind": "observed contract mismatch (static control flow, not executed)",
      "source": "services/node-agent/internal/migrationcontext/p02_evaluate_internal.go:263 checks len(c.in.signatures) <= 16 inside the 04_SIGNATURE stage (SIGNATURE, bounded-signature-tuple-table); p02_inputs_internal.go:1067 only refuses more than 4096 tuples in the pre-stage budget (OWNERSHIP at 01_ANCHOR). anchor() (:104-118) does not check the table size.",
      "contract": "Accepted design candidate_model.py:173 (Rev2 and Rev3): need(type(a.signatures) is frozenset and len(a.signatures)<=16,'OWNERSHIP','immutable-signature-table') inside _anchor, so the first refusal is OWNERSHIP at 01_ANCHOR with an empty passed prefix. Root grant msg_ccd8401cb2c5: 'Use exact accepted STAGES/first-reason order'.",
      "validCase": "Benign C01 fixture plus 16 more well-formed tuples (17 total; the matching tuple is still a member). Design: OWNERSHIP / 01_ANCHOR / immutable-signature-table, passed []. 08e0: passes 01_ANCHOR, 02_SOURCES, 03_ENVELOPE, 03_PAYLOAD, 03_C2, then refuses SIGNATURE / 04_SIGNATURE / bounded-signature-tuple-table. Any count 17..4096 behaves the same way; 16 is accepted by both.",
      "impact": "Fail-closed in both versions; no acceptance difference; public refusal is the same constant. Only the private first cause/stage and the earlier prefix differ, and up to 4096 budget-bounded tuples are frozen before the refusal. No test covers counts 17..4096, which is how this went unnoticed.",
      "minimalCorrection": "Refuse len(prerequisites.signatures) > 16 as OWNERSHIP / 01_ANCHOR / immutable-signature-table before freezing (p02BudgetInputs or the p02Evaluate pre-check). The 04 check may stay as a redundant guard. Add a 17-tuple test with an exact empty prefix and a 16-tuple control.",
      "optionalProbe": "optional_probe_signature_table_bound_test.go.txt: inert DATA, NOT_RUN, not needed for this verdict; Root may run it on an isolated 08e0 checkout if execution evidence is wanted."
    }
  ],
  "info": [
    {"id": "D04-I1", "text": "Order of refusals when several sources are missing in 02_SOURCES (p02_evaluate_internal.go:121-124). Go checks ticket&&clock (TIME) before measurement (INSTALLATION). The design checks h5 (INSTALLATION) before clock (TIME). So ticket present + clock and H5 both missing gives TIME in Go but INSTALLATION in the design. Separately, the pre-stage budget refusal (OWNERSHIP) comes before the nil-capsule check (ANCHOR); both are 01_ANCHOR. With a single missing source the two agree, and the design's targeted cases are single-fault. Fail-closed; optional to align."},
    {"id": "D04-I2", "text": "Go is stricter than the design in several places, all fail-closed. Lifecycle floor must be > 0 (:549). Clock, lifecycle, ticket and H5 times must be in the epoch domain (:571-580). Ticket id must be non-empty (:562). Raw coverage evidence, H5 evidence and the artifact must be non-empty (:418, :493, :482). Readback uses a structured token bound to capsule/generation/selector/scope/record identity/version/ticket/H5 digest, instead of the design's opaque v0==v1 (:587). rootChoiceSHA256 is computed over the raw H3-EA evidence bytes instead of trusting a claimed field (:418; this moves toward P02R2-I2, but binding those bytes to the typed statement is still the producer's job, as the README says). C2 is ASCII-only, which is equivalent after schema validation because every authority-scope string is printable ASCII. None of these turns a design refusal into acceptance. Some could refuse inputs the design would accept (for example floor 0). A future contract delta should list them explicitly."},
    {"id": "D04-I3", "text": "README.md:175-176 (frozen published bytes) still says 'At this WIP checkpoint its Go tests are NOT_RUN'. Root actually ran 23 top-level / 228 subtests on these exact bytes before publication. The sentence is time-stamped as a WIP checkpoint and points toward less assurance, not more, but it is stale. The publication cut kept the 14 bytes frozen; update it in the next code cut. Root's original receipts are authoritative."},
    {"id": "D04-I4", "text": "Precision note for P02R3-I1. p02Expectation kinds 'a'/'o' carry no content (p02_canonical_internal.go:21-24), so a present non-empty array or object expectation cannot be expressed in the typed capsule. It can only appear as a raw-vs-typed mismatch, which refuses ANCHOR at 01. Present empty []/{} and int/bool/null/empty-string/129-byte values reach 05 closed-independent-effective-verdict-expectation, and non-printable values refuse at 01, as P02R3-I1 recorded. Fail-closed."}
  ],
  "verifiedWithoutFinding": {
    "codec": "p02_codec_internal.go. The byte budget is checked before parser allocation (:375) and before each stage copy (evaluate :128/:183/:482). Depth 32 and 100000 nodes (keys count as nodes), the same as design strict_json walk. Strings are printable ASCII 32..126 only, so BOM, control, non-ASCII, invalid-UTF-8 and surrogate input is refused. \\u escapes must decode to printable characters and are then caught by the exact round-trip. Keys are strictly increasing, which rejects duplicates and unsorted keys; escaped key aliases and \\/ fail the round-trip. Integers: no fraction, exponent, -0 or leading zero, and |n| <= 2^53-1 via n > (S-d)/10. Kinds b/i/n/s/o/a are distinct, so bool is never an int. No whitespace or trailing bytes are accepted. In C2 mode the encoder escapes & < > in keys and values with lowercase \\u00XX, matching the design's c2 and Go Marshal. Imports are bytes/encoding/hex/unicode/utf8/time only; there is no encoding/json, interface, callback or new dependency.",
    "schemas": "reviewer_schema_compare.py.txt maps all 168 generated validator functions back to the three immutable Rev2 schemas (envelope 60d6c825, payload 02d0b30f, authority scope ccae1398): 296 schema nodes, 0 differences. Every one of the 50 objects has required == properties and additionalProperties false, so Go's exact-count closed objects are equivalent. Two seeded mutants (grants maxItems 513, renamed review key) were detected, which shows the comparator is not vacuous. Pattern ids 1-6 are equivalent to the regexes; id 0 is validSelector (policy.go:83), equivalent to ^[A-Za-z0-9_-]{1,128}. All envelope strings are bounded at <= 32768 by schema, so the design's 65536 envelope string cap gives the same FORMAT 03_ENVELOPE result.",
    "stageReasons": "reviewer_stage_reasons.py.txt: the 20 stage methods, in order, use only reasons allowed by design STAGES (07 uses CI and PROVENANCE). The 14 reason IDs match. The pre-stage budget refusal OWNERSHIP@01_ANCHOR is allowed.",
    "joins": "Compared with design _anchor.._readback one by one, and all equivalent apart from D04-L1/I1/I2. Capsule: closed by the typed round-trip, with expectation presence required at 01, format/purpose and UID domain. Signature: SCOPE binding (selector/scope/capsule hash/generation/anchor) comes before the exact tuple: format, purpose, domain, key, capsule, generation, selector, scope, anchor, record version, request binding, and full domain+NUL+canonical body/signer bytes plus signature bytes. No body-only or digest-only form is accepted, and the tests cover this. Key interval. Payload selector/version/verifier/ordered runIDs. Eight component digests from exact raw/C2 bytes plus independent source constants. Reviews: original rows equal H3; origin purpose and identity; coverage source/tree/C2 review set; bijective outcome map; ordered complete unique partition; preserved targets; independent reviewed==current part bytes; DIRECT iff target==source; effective target; exact capsule literal 1..128; publication not in outcomes ∪ originals ∪ parts (I2: may equal the source SHA); fact joins; coverage/equivalence/raw-evidence digests. Source facts are all 38 non-echo fields, plus the VCS join. CI: runs equal H3 records (this binds repository/ref/event/workflow/correlation/attempt/jobs/steps); head and conclusion; required/optional are disjoint and non-empty and form an exact bijection with the actual steps; required steps succeed and optional ones succeed or are skipped. Artifact zip size and digest are checked before the copy. H5: raw bytes equal the typed record; component/pid/generation/UID/root; five H5-vs-H3 fields; H3 approved-vs-installation closure. Status, version/floor/record identity, ticket/request/echo, and freshness equal the design.",
    "projection": "07 has the same primary-CI selection (not first-green), the same review/scope/head/VCS/run-membership joins, grant interval/domain, unique (role, C2 scope, key), exactly two PC2/PC4 members bound to the independent DER/CA/scope/SPKI, and a node-leaf grant per member. All 41 policyData leaves are assigned. Provenance receipt/lock/link come from H3 source facts and RunningExecutable from H5. Verifier source/artifact come from H3 (artifact = executable binarySHA256; ArtifactDigest = zip). The 5 runningData fields come from H5 only. NotBefore/NotAfter use exact time.Unix(n,0).UTC(); CI IDs use canonical decimal. Output is owned: fresh unhex bytes, copied maps, new scope maps, and freezePolicy deep copies.",
    "boundary": "p02Evaluate has no non-test caller. The seam constructs no InstalledPolicy, History or binding, and publicRefusal is the constant TrustUnknown. effect_gate_test.go adds only time.Unix and time.Time.UTC (two of the four objects the grant allowed), and p02_effect_test.go checks alias/method-expression controls plus Now/Since/NewTimer/Local/ed25519.Sign/foreign-write denials. K1 policy.go/ports/history/k1_bridge are unchanged (Root blob check)."
  },
